                        <field name="dc_description">In the 4th century AD, the rhetoric teacher Gaius Marius Victorinus wrote explanatory notes on Cicero’s  De inventione. In the third quarter of the 15th century, these were copied in a completely uniform script, probably in Frace. The scholar Johannes Heynlin from Basel bequeathed this manuscript, together with the other books in his vast library, to the Carthusian Monastery of Basel. The manuscript shows no signs of use. </field>
